 "result": "Confirmed: previously, garbage-collecting the `MaybeStripAnsi` wrapper would close the underlying buffer (e.g. real `sys.stdout.buffer`); now it stays open.\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed `MaybeStripAnsi` in `src/click/_termui_impl.py` (used by `get_pager_file`/`echo_via_pager`) so it no longer closes the underlying stream \u2014 which is often the real `stdout`/pager stdin, not something it owns \u2014 when the wrapper is garbage collected. Added a `__del__` override that detaches instead of closing, mirroring the existing `_NonClosingTextIOWrapper` pattern in `_compat.py`. Also added a `CHANGES.rst` entry. Full test suite (1562 passed) confirms no regressions, and a manual GC test confirms the underlying buffer now stays open.",
